{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:13cb486556250256d774ef09c5c73594", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 8, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Fixed. The script now:\n\n1. Produces zero output when `logs/` is empty (the glob is left unexpanded and the redirect fails silently - cron was mailing on this every hour), and\n2. Prints exactly one `processed: <filename>` line per log file, with no extra `($n lines)` noise.\n\nThe `wc -l` counting isn't needed since the required output format is just the filename, so I dropped it along with its `echo`. Verified output matches the required format.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:18d63bfcb62141318c21099bb34ef5b7"}
